   "source": [
    "# Section 01 -- Define the target & population\n",
    "\n",
    "**Section question:** How many loans defaulted (is_bad=1), and what's the LGD distribution when we compute recovery rates?\n",
    "\n",
    "| # | Step |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 1.1 | Compute LGD targets on charged-off loans |\n",
    "| 1.2 | Population sanity checks |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.1 Compute LGD targets\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why:** LGD is defined as `1 - (total_recovery / exposure_at_default)`. For Lending Club loans, EAD is the principal balance outstanding at the moment of default.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How:** Load the raw Lending Club data (from Phase 0's DuckDB), filter to `is_bad=1`, compute recovery facts (`total_rec_prncp`) and EAD (`funded_amnt - total_pymnt`).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answers:** What's the population size and LGD distribution?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load raw data with recovery facts from Phase 0 DuckDB\n",
    "con = duckdb.connect(DUCKDB_FILE, read_only=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Query: filtered, windowed population where is_bad=1, with recovery facts\n",
    "sql_defaulted = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    id,\n",
    "    loan_amnt,\n",
    "    issue_d,\n",
    "    term,\n",
    "    grade,\n",
    "    funded_amnt,\n",
    "    total_pymnt,\n",
    "    total_rec_prncp,\n",
    "    total_rec_int,\n",
    "    loan_status,\n",
    "    last_pymnt_amnt,\n",
    "    last_pymnt_d,\n",
    "    is_bad\n",
    "FROM windowed\n",
    "WHERE is_bad = 1\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df_defaulted = con.sql(sql_defaulted).df()\n",
    "print(f\"Charged-off loans (is_bad=1): {len(df_defaulted):,}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute LGD\n",
    "df_defaulted['ead'] = df_defaulted['funded_amnt'] - df_defaulted['total_pymnt']\n",
    "df_defaulted['recovery'] = df_defaulted['total_rec_prncp']\n",
    "df_defaulted['lgd'] = 1.0 - (df_defaulted['recovery'] / df_defaulted['ead']).clip(lower=-np.inf, upper=1.0)\n",
    "df_defaulted['lgd'] = df_defaulted['lgd'].clip(0, 1.0)  # bound to [0, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nLGD Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(df_defaulted['lgd'].describe())\n",
    "print(f\"\\nLGD > 1.0 (edge cases): {(df_defaulted['lgd'] > 1.0).sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"LGD < 0 (full recovery + more): {(df_defaulted['lgd'] < 0).sum()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result:** **240,885 charged-off loans** with computed LGD targets. LGD range **[0.00, 1.00]** (clipped to bound). Mean LGD **~0.73** (73% loss on average); median **~0.82** (82% loss)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.2 Population sanity checks\n",
    "\n",
