    "# Section 08 -- Governance & caveats\n",
    "\n",
    "**Section question:** What assumptions underpin this model, and what's left for Phase 3?\n",
    "\n",
    "| # | Step |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 8.1 | Known caveats |\n",
    "| 8.2 | Recommended next steps |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8.1 Known caveats\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **LGD is only for defaults:** This model is calibrated only on charged-off loans. Non-defaulted loans have no realized recovery and do not contribute to LGD estimation (they contribute to Phase 3 ECL via PD × LGD).\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Unsecured personal lending:** Lending Club loans are unsecured with no collateral. LGD variation is driven entirely by borrower characteristics and loan structure, not by asset value.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Historical recovery data:** Recovery facts (`total_rec_prncp`, `total_rec_int`) reflect Lending Club's published historical file. Future recovery may differ due to macro conditions, changes in collection practices, etc.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **No cure/prepayment modeling:** A loan with status='Fully Paid' (no default) has realized LGD=0. A loan with status='Charged Off' has realized LGD computed from recovery. This model does not explicitly model the timing or probability of cure—it treats cure as a binary outcome (either default or don't).\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Segmentation assumptions:** Segment-level validation (by grade, term) assumes that per-segment performance is stable over time. Regulatory stress scenarios may violate this assumption.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 8.2 Recommended next steps\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Phase 3 ECL:** Use this LGD model + Phase 1 PD model to compute expected credit loss per loan and aggregate to portfolio level.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Stressed LGD:** Develop LGD scenarios (e.g., recession impact on recovery rates) for stress testing and capital modeling.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Model monitoring:** Track actual-vs-predicted LGD on new charged-offs quarterly; flag if segment-level performance drifts > 5% from this baseline.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Partial recovery modeling:** If Lending Club data permits, model recovery timing and partial recoveries separately (multi-state approach) rather than treating recovery as a point estimate."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 08 -- Output Interpretation & Governance Impact\n",
    "\n",
    "**Governance complete.** The LGD model is production-ready for Phase 3 ECL computation, with known caveats documented. Recovery is inherently unpredictable (AUC 0.62 vs. 0.72 for PD); the model's utility is in ranking loans by expected recovery, not in absolute predictions."
